"gracious loser" face?

267
00:10:21,413 --> 00:10:24,040
Yeah.
Very nice.

268
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:26,126
Now, remember, if you
win, you have to hug me.

269
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:27,127
You hug me.
Okay.

270
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,421
Can I squeeze your ass?

271
00:10:30,464 --> 00:10:31,423
On TV?

272
00:10:31,465 --> 00:10:32,424
Yeah.

273
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:33,425
Yeah.

274
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:35,093
Okay!

275
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:37,345
In the category of Favorite
Returning Male Character

276
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:38,679
the nominees are...

277
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:42,976
John Wheeler
from General Hospital

278
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:46,980
Gavin Graham
from The Young and the Restless

279
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:50,942
Duncan Harrington from Passions

280
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:55,196
and Joey Tribbiani
from Days of our Lives

281
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:59,618
and the Soapie goes to...

282
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:00,785
Gavin Graham

283
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:02,245
from The Young and the Restless.

284
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:04,623
What the...?!

285
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,916
( music playing )

286
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:16,926
for Favorite Supporting Actress

287
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:18,178
is Joey Tribbiani
from Days of Our Lives.

288
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:20,096
Whoo!

289
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:22,474
( applause and music )

290
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,813
( in a monotone ):
Any one of
the brilliant actresses

291
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,649
nominated for this award tonight

292
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:32,025
deserves to take it home.

293
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:34,152
Unfortunately, only one can.

294
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:36,863
( scoffing softly )

295
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:40,241
The nominees for Favorite
Supporting Actress are...

296
00:11:40,283 --> 00:11:41,826
from Passions, Erin Gough...

297
00:11:46,623 --> 00:11:49,000
from One Life to Live,
Mary Lauren Bishop...

298
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:52,212
( cutting off applause):
from All My Children,
Sarah Renee...

299
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:55,131
and from Days of Our Lives,
Jessica Ashley.

300
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:57,716
And the winner is...

301
00:11:57,758 --> 00:12:00,595
Jessica Ashley
from Days of Our Lives.

302
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:03,181
Oh, uh, unfortunately

303
00:12:03,223 --> 00:12:04,932
Jessica couldn't be
with us tonight

304
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:06,601
so I'll be accepting
this award

305
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:08,603
on her behalf.

306
00:12:12,524 --> 00:12:15,443
And I'm sure that Jessica...

307
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:17,904
would like to thank my parents

308
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:20,156
who always
believed in me.

309
00:12:20,198 --> 00:12:22,200
She'd also like to thank
my friends

310
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:26,413
Chandler, Monica, Ross,
Phoebe and Rachel

311
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:28,373
who's sitting right there.

312
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,460
( microphone goes dead )

313
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:43,971
Joey, why did we have
to rush out of there so fast?

314
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,224
Rach, we had to get
out of there because...

315
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:48,476
look what I won! Ha-ha-ha-ha!

316
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:53,565
Oh, my God, you
stole her award.

317
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:57,193
No, no, oh, no.
I'm accepting it on her behalf.

318
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:59,153
Well... Joey, I don't
think you know

319
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,614
what "behalf" means.

320
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:01,864
Sure I do.

321
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:05,285
It's a verb,
as in "I behalf'n it."

322
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:08,871
Joey...

323
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:11,666
you have got
to take this back.
Why?

324
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,834
I should've won one,
and I really wanted it.

325
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:16,296
She didn't even care enough
to come to the thing.

326
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:18,590
It could also be a Grammy.

327
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:23,470
No, Joey.

328
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:25,472
Come on, Rach.
No one saw me take it.

329
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,474
There was a whole table
full of them.

330
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:30,184
Do you really want an award
that you didn't win?

331
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,019
No. I want an award I did win

332
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:34,188
but nobody's given me
any of those.

333
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:37,942
Plus, okay, Rach,
if I put it up there-- right?--

334
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:39,736
when people come over,
they'll see it

335
00:13:39,778 --> 00:13:41,321
and they'll think I won it.

336
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:44,365
Joey, it says "Best
Supporting Actress."

337
00:13:44,407 --> 00:13:46,993
I can scratch that right off.

338
00:13:47,034 --> 00:13:48,745
Joey, no, this is wrong.

339
00:13:48,787 --> 00:13:50,622
You have to take it back.

340
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:53,832
Okay? You don't want
to win an award this way.

341
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:55,502
You're very talented

342
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:58,546
and someday you're going
to win one of these for real

343
00:13:58,588 --> 00:14:00,881
and that one is going
to mean something.

344
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:04,843
All right.
All right?

345
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:06,721
Thank you.

346
00:14:06,763 --> 00:14:08,348
I'll take it back tomorrow.

347
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:09,890
Thank you.

348
00:14:21,361 --> 00:14:23,029
If I can't have it,
you can't have it.

349
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:24,322
( grunts angrily )

350
00:14:30,495 --> 00:14:32,121
Professor Geller?

351
00:14:32,163 --> 00:14:34,873
Yes, Mr. Lewis,
how can I help you?

352
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:38,877
I know I didn't do well
on my midterms and stuff, but...

353
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:41,798
I was kind of hoping
you could change my grade.

354
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,467
And why exactly
would I do that?

355
00:14:44,509 --> 00:14:46,845
'Cause I'm in love with you.

356
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:51,599
What?

357
00:14:51,641 --> 00:14:55,520
Yeah. I'm all...
in love with you and stuff.

358
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:59,232
So could you change my grade?

359
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:01,359
No!

360
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:03,611
Well, why not?
You changed Ned's grade.

361
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:05,572
Well, that's different, okay?

362
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:07,948
Because he was actually
in love with me.

363
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:09,283
No, he's not.

364
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:11,411
He's totally yanking your chain.

365
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:13,996
He's done this
with three other teachers.

366
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,249
What?

367
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,042
He's got a girlfriend.

368
00:15:18,084 --> 00:15:22,839
I can't believe someone
would do that for a grade.

369
00:15:22,881 --> 00:15:25,842
I know. It's awful.

370
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,095
I love you.

371
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,391
Hey, have you
seen Chandler?

372
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:34,559
No. Why?

373
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:35,852
'Cause I just
keep thinking

374
00:15:35,894 --> 00:15:37,562
about all these things

375
00:15:37,604 --> 00:15:39,814
that I'm not going to have,
and it's freaking me out.

376
00:15:39,856 --> 00:15:41,524
I don't know what
to do about it.

377
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:42,942
Okay, don't sweat it.

378
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:44,736
Chandler is nowhere around

379
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:46,654
so go ahead,
get it out of your system.

380
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:47,864
That guy's cute.

381
00:15:48,907 --> 00:15:51,242
Phoebe, come on,
I'm serious.

382
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:54,036
I've just got to talk
to him about all this.

383
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,831
That is the last thing
you want to do.

384
00:15:56,873 --> 00:15:58,124
Why?

385
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:00,877
Because you're marrying him.

386
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:03,838
You got to help me
out here, Pheebs.

387
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,465
All right,
I've never been engaged

388
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:07,174
and I've never
really been married

389
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:10,261
but I can only tell you
what my mother told me.

390
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:12,388
Whenever you have
doubts or fears

391
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:14,557
or anxieties
about a relationship

392
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:17,602
do not communicate them
to your husband.

393
00:16:17,644 --> 00:16:21,272
So, I'm not supposed to
share my doubts and fears

394
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:25,610
with the guy I'm
going to spend the
rest of my life with?

395
00:16:25,652 --> 00:16:26,903
That is correct.

396
00:16:26,945 --> 00:16:29,363
Yes, you're supposed
to take all that stuff

397
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:31,741
and put it in a little box
in your mind

398
00:16:31,783 --> 00:16:33,493
and then lock it up tight.

399
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:36,287
Your mother told you this?
Yes.

400
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:38,498
The woman that got married
a bunch of times

401
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:40,374
and killed herself
when you were 13?

402
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,962
Oh, my God, you're right.
All right, go.

403
00:16:44,002 --> 00:16:45,087
Go tell Chandler.

404
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:46,881
Hurry, before it's too late.

405
00:16:46,923 --> 00:16:48,174
Wait! No!

406
00:16:48,215 --> 00:16:49,550
Does this also mean

407
00:16:49,592 --> 00:16:51,970
that putting out
doesn't get you love?

408
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:59,769
I cannot believe I'm going
to meet Jessica Ashley.

409
00:16:59,811 --> 00:17:01,437
Wait, wait. Please...

410
00:17:01,479 --> 00:17:02,689
be cool, okay?

411
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,190
I work with this woman.

412
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:05,316
Okay, I'm totally cool.

413
00:17:05,358 --> 00:17:06,317
Okay.

414
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,902
Come in.

415
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:11,155
Hey, Jessica.

416
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:12,824
Hey, Jess.

417
00:17:12,866 --> 00:17:14,993
Uh, this is my friend Rachel.

418
00:17:15,033 --> 00:17:15,869
Hi.

419
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:17,829
What's up?

420
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,958
Uh, listen,
here's your trophy.

421
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,501
I accepted it for you.

422
00:17:23,543 --> 00:17:25,712
Oh, my God, I won?

423
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,881
Do you have any idea
what this means?

424
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,885
Wow, that-that's it?
You're not going...

425
00:17:31,926 --> 00:17:34,470
you're not going to put it
on your shelf or anything?

426
00:17:34,512 --> 00:17:36,597
No. I try to save that
for real awards.

427
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:38,098
Now, if you'll excuse me.

428
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:42,061
Hmm...

429
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:44,104
Take it back?
Absolutely.

430
00:17:48,902 --> 00:17:50,904
Yeah, you do.

431
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:54,657
Honey?
Hmm?

432
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:56,826
As we get closer
to the wedding

433
00:17:56,868 --> 00:18:00,413
is there anything that you'd
like to talk about or share?

434
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:03,750
Okay, well, I think
the centerpieces are too big.

435
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:06,210
You're wrong.
The centerpieces are fine.

436
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:10,172
Do you ever get scared at all?

437
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:12,425
Kind of. They're really big.

438
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:16,387
I mean, does it ever
freak you out that-that...

439
00:18:16,429 --> 00:18:19,515
you're never going to be
with anybody new again?

440
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:21,350
What?

441
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:24,437
Just... I love you so much.

442
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:26,773
It's just that
sometimes it bothers me

443
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:29,149
that I'm never going
to have that feeling...

444
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:31,903
you know, when you meet someone
for the first time

445
00:18:31,945 --> 00:18:33,905
and it's new and exciting.

446
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:35,782
You know that rush?

447
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:37,825
No.

448
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:39,786
Now, see, when I
first meet somebody

449
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:43,998
it's, uh, it's mostly panic,
anxiety and a...

450
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,959
great deal of sweating.

451
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,294
Okay, but, all right,
you're a guy.

452
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,254
Does it not freak you out

453
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:53,716
that you're never going
to sleep with anybody else?

454
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:56,094
Sleeping with somebody new.

455
00:18:56,135 --> 00:19:00,723
Anxiety, panic and, I'm afraid,
even more sweating.

456
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:03,267
Even with me?

457
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:04,894
I was dangerously dehydrated

458
00:19:04,936 --> 00:19:07,647
during the first six months
of our relationship.

459
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:09,899
Look...

460
00:19:09,941 --> 00:19:11,776
for me, the rush is knowing

461
00:19:11,818 --> 00:19:14,946
that we are going to be together
for the rest of our lives.

462
00:19:14,988 --> 00:19:18,032
Really?
Well, yeah.

463
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:20,827
But now that I know that
you're having these thoughts

464
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:23,121
we're back to panic, anxiety,
and, uh

465
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:26,540
I'm definitely going to need
some kind of sports drink.

466
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:28,167
Come here.

467
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,627
Come here.

468
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:32,463
Sweetie, you don't
have to worry.

469
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:34,298
No. Besides, you know what?

470
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:37,259
I'm going to have a lot
of new things with you:

471
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:40,638
the first time we buy a house,
our first kid

472
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,222
our first grandkid.

473
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:44,767
Water! Water! Water!

474
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:49,689
Uh, Mr. Morse, can I speak
to you for a moment?

475
00:19:51,858 --> 00:19:55,653
That was a great
lecture today.

476
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:57,071
Did you get a little haircut?

477
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:58,823
Mm-hmm, yeah, yeah.
Do you like it?

478
00:19:58,865 --> 00:20:00,867
Do you love it?

479
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:05,329
I just want you to know that
I'm changing your grade back.

480
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:07,915
What? Why?

481
00:20:07,957 --> 00:20:10,501
Because I know what you're
trying to pull here, okay?

482
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:11,836
It's not going to work.

483
00:20:11,878 --> 00:20:14,172
I'm not trying
to pull anything.

484
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,924
Look, I love you, dude.

485
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:20,094
You know what?
I'm not even going to
talk about this, okay?

486
00:20:20,136 --> 00:20:21,679
This little thing is over.

487
00:20:21,721 --> 00:20:23,389
I know you have
a girlfriend.

488
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,100
Okay? Yeah, and I know
about the other professors.

489
00:20:26,142 --> 00:20:28,352
How do you think that
makes me feel, Ned?

490
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:30,270
You used me!

491
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:33,066
You don't love me,
and you never did!

492
00:20:35,109 --> 00:20:39,072
Ah, Professor Winston,
Professor Frederickson.

493
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:42,575
I'll be right with you.

494
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:45,452
Don't make this worse,
and I'll give you a "C."

495
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:46,787
Shall we?

496
00:20:52,543 --> 00:20:54,378
Rach?

497
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,463
I'll be out
in a second.

498
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:57,924
Mmm.

499
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:03,137
It's just so unexpected.

500
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:05,723
( laughing ):
I... I, uh...

501
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:08,559
Well, it's... I'll tell you,
it's just such an honor

502
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:10,978
to just be nominated...

503
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:14,565
for a Nobel prize.

504
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:20,238
And, you know, to win one
for a massage, oh...

505
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:24,033
especially after having just won
a Tony award for Best Actress...

506
00:21:24,075 --> 00:21:26,077
We have to go.
Our reservations are at 8:00.

507
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:27,745
In Reservations at 8:00...

508
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,747
by Neil Simon.

509
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:31,749
Thank you, thank you, Neil.

510
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:33,918
Thank you for the words.

511
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,586
Okay, honey, you can
finish this later.

512
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:37,213
We're going to be late.
We got to go.

513
00:21:37,255 --> 00:21:39,006
No, please, don't
play the music.

514
00:21:39,048 --> 00:21:40,758
I just have
one more thing.
Okay.

515
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:43,803
Live from New York,
it's Saturday Night!

